 "notes": [
  "three rows come off a face that publishes 57 numbers in the gated quantity's unit and none of them is the quantity: a decoy is worse than an absence because it invites substitution, and the tolerance a reader would compute from those decoys spans 1.5 orders of magnitude (6e-11 at the smallest published count to 1.92e-09 at the largest)",
  "two rows come off a face that covers a day on which nothing was compared -- zero positive numbers outside the tolerance constant, every per-trader detail list empty -- so calling their absence a schema gap would be the same artefact E315 avoided one level down",
  "on that second face the identifier is a quoted payload key in the producer and has zero instances today: the requirement is met for any day that carries a comparison, and the face does not say which kind of day it is",
  "a unit word is not a quantity: `base_draws` names the unit of the gated quantity without being one of its magnitudes, and counting it would repeat the writer-side error of treating a name as a measurement"
